Some time back I was playing an old PC version of Hack 1.0.3 on a machine 
connected to a CD-ROM drive, and it crashed mysteriously (not the normal 
way Hack crashes with the dungeon collapsing or whatever) and my 
tombstone said I had been killed by a CD-ROM driver. To wit "Killed by a 
SONY MSCDEX_2.0.1 .."" something to that effect. It wouldn't even all fit 
on the tombstone! (Wish i still had the screen dump I made of that one.)

Well my curiosity about this is mostly academic since lately I've been 
playing NetHack 3.0 and it seems to mostly work fine except for the 
occasional hang, but I thought I'd throw it out and see if anyone else 
encountered such a weird bug (before or since.) Obviously some strange 
software conflict caused Hack to interpret the driver code as a monster. 
i never was able to reproduce the incident. 

I'm not really savvy with source code, but maybe somebody who is could 
find clues there...

